{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The radius of a cylindrical box is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches and the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches. The number of inches that may be added to either the radius or the height to give the same nonzero increase in volume is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e1a8f32679366974a9fa51e29e95c7dec560ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5\\frac {1}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{any number} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{non-existent} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"605\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of inches increased. We can set up an equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/85244f9a7205dd77fd62da4dedf132ea43206b5c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8^2 \\times (3+x)=(8+x)^2\\times 3\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Expanding gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d62b6db268f21a8f2e8fe2e0166098edb6a23d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2+48x+192=64x+192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"229\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Combining like terms gives the quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4efcc28ecb967ed790f7e58a18ba4ececcdf90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2-16x=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Factoring out an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b42bd19aca3095ee692771664a47a4164ffe38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(3x-16)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>So either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b20224dfed4a26ef364dfb505a45eb176500138b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x-16=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The first equation is not possible, because the problem states that the value has to be non-zero. The second equation gives the answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a50fafc708655095939e398a55bd263302ddb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{5\\frac{1}{3}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"71\" height=\"48\" /> Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/5178df2ddd498a2b2eaa255413e1fda543664f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1951 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1951\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"